Convention: lowercase acts on the file under the cursor;     
UPPERCASE extends to the dir / every marked file.            
Marks are a worklist: a bulk action consumes them on success 
and keeps them on failure (fix + retry). `a` (add) keeps them
for the follow-up commit. `x` clears them all.               
                                                             
Navigation
──────────
  Vertical: arrows / jk move within the pane. Horizontal is a    
  ranger/yazi axis: → goes deeper (expand, then cross into the   
  right pane), ← goes shallower (fold / walk up; from a right    
  pane it returns to the left). Ctrl+h/l/j/k jump panes directly.
                                                                   j / k       cursor down / up
  l / →       expand dir; nothing to expand → right pane
  h / ←       collapse / up (tree); right pane → back left
  ~           collapse all, jump to root (tree)
  g / G       top / bottom
  PgUp/PgDn   scroll page (also C-u / C-d)
  enter       select + jump to right pane (yazi-style)
  C-h / C-←   focus left pane
  C-l / C-→   focus right pane
  C-j / C-↓   focus console
  C-k / C-↑   back to panes from console
  tab         cycle focused panel
  /           fuzzy search files
  q           quit lazycvs (inside a dialog: close it)

Tabs
────
  1           Files — tree+filelist OR tree+diff preview
  2           Favorites — pinned directories
  3           Staged — files marked for commit
  4           History — revisions of the selected file

  Bootstrap: `lazycvs init` in an empty dir to check out a fresh
module from a CVSROOT (TUI prompts for root + module).        

File actions
────────────
  d           diff (working vs base revision)
  c           commit cursor file (or marked files)
  C-e         commit message in $EDITOR (while input focused)
  a           add cursor file (?-status) to CVS
  r           revert cursor file (bulk in Staged tab)
  B           restore .lazycvs-backup (marked / dir subtree / cursor)
  D           remove (single file or marked set)
  i           ignore — add pattern to .cvsignore
  e           edit in $EDITOR
  E           external diff tool (config.diff_tool)
  M           external merge tool (conflict files)
  o           open in OS default app
  C-e         edit in $EDITOR (picker-style alias of e)
  C-o         alternate opener (config [editor] alt_open)
  C-r         reveal in Finder / file manager
  C-y         copy absolute path to clipboard
  space       mark/unmark
  A           mark/unmark every changed file in dir
  x           clear ALL marks (in console: clear log)
  + / -       add/remove from favorites

View & filters
──────────────
  v           layout: Files (tree+list) ↔ Detail (tree+preview)
  f           list mode: flat → sub → tree
  F           status filter: all → * → M → C → ? → all
  I           toggle hide-ignored on both panes
  t           jump list to tree mode

CVS
───
  s           status refresh (dry-run + scan, parallel)
  u           update (cvs update -d -P)
  U           force update (cvs update -C — overwrite!)
  H           recent repo changes for dir + subdirs (all users)
             cvs history; window: history_days (default 7d).
             Enter on a row opens that file's History tab.  

History tab
───────────
  enter       show revision content
  d           show diff vs previous revision
  p           toggle side-by-side diff
  b           blame view
  w           compare vs working copy
  R           restore selected revision into working copy
  space       anchor revision for two-rev comparison
  E           open the selected pair in the external diff tool
  M           merge the selected pair into the working copy
  B           restore the file's .lazycvs-backup (e.g. undo a pair merge)
  < / >       horizontal scroll in diff content
  esc         cancel comparison mode

  Top row is the working copy when modified — diff there shows
local changes vs repository.                                

Console
───────
  F           cycle filter: compact → verbose → errors → slow
  + / -       grow / shrink the console panel (when focused)
  x           clear panel (session log file keeps everything)

  Every cvs command and file operation (rm / mv / backup) is                 
also appended to /Users/max/Library/Application Support/lazycvs/lazycvs.log

Status codes
────────────
  M   Locally Modified — you changed this file
  U   Update available — newer revision on server
  C   Conflict — both you and server changed it
  ?   Untracked — not in CVS
  I   Ignored — matched by .cvsignore
  A   Added — scheduled for commit
  R   Removed — scheduled for deletion
